## Attribution

### camera/
The method and the configuration layers come from ocewers' work on this same
laptop:

    https://github.com/ocewers/x1c14-camera-imx471

His README describes the layers this directory follows: kernel modules,
libcamera and PipeWire, v4l2-relayd, then tuning. He calls it an interim
workaround until kernel 7.3.

The imx471 sensor module itself is Ben BJD's, installed from the AUR:

    https://github.com/BenBJD/imx471-dkms          upstream
    https://aur.archlinux.org/packages/imx471-dkms-git   AUR, maintained by dbav892

The scripts here are mine: they apply those layers without modifying a
package-owned file, and revert.sh takes them back off.

### typec-ucsi/
The retry patch is mine, written against drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ and sent to
linux-usb. Heikki Krogerus reviewed and acked it.

    v1      https://lore.kernel.org/linux-usb/20260815005724.8741-1-jacob@riff.dk/
    v2      https://lore.kernel.org/linux-usb/20260824173536.2395830-1-jacob@riff.dk/
    review  https://lore.kernel.org/linux-usb/apVQVU4fPNC6675K@black.igk.intel.com/

The module build and the DKMS wrapper are mine. The code being patched is the
kernel's, thus this directory is GPL-2.0.

### touchpad/input-host.lua
The idea of a custom libinput velocity curve under Hyprland, and the shape of
it, come from a gist by Daniel Lemky:

    https://gist.github.com/DanielLemky/671889f0eee518e3690cca18a0ad648e

His values are for an M1 MacBook trackpad and were far too slow on this panel.
The numbers here were measured with evtest and tuned on this hardware. The
method is his; the values are not.

